Conflicts: brcmfmac-awdl-dkms
Description: AirDrop over firmware-native AWDL on Apple Silicon Macs (opt in)
 The userspace for AirDrop over the AWDL link that the Broadcom Wi-Fi firmware
 of Apple Silicon Macs implements and Aurora's brcmfmac exposes as awdl0: the
 omdrop-awdl helpers that create awdl0 and open discoverability windows, and
 the omdrop-plugin receiver, run as a user service.
 .
 Nothing runs after installation: awdl0.service, awdl-warmup.service and the
 user's airdrop-receiver.service are installed disabled.
 .
 Recommended: network-manager keeps awdl0 unmanaged and settles the Wi-Fi MAC
 first; python3-pil makes the thumbnail an iPhone needs before it shows a
 prompt. bluez, python3-dbus and python3-gi send the advert that wakes a
 nearby Apple device; keyutils holds the optional cached Apple identity.
